WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.660
Phillip: Communication is all about giving,
receiving, and sharing information but this must

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.420
be done clearly and effectively to be of value.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.680
Different forms of communication are suitable
for different occasions, and there's no

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.649
one way that's better than all the others.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:20.720
Maddy: So, how can you achieve clear
and effective communication using

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.540
the main forms of communication?

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.689
Let’s look at these whilst remembering
that different methods will often

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.430
be combined in different ways.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.230
Phillip: Written communication, this includes
emails, handwritten memos, typed letters, digital

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.680
messages, SMS messages, and much more besides.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.470
When using written communication, you need
to be precise, clear, and unambiguous.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.629
Make sure you're being explicit with
what you want to communicate, and

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.189
don't leave it to interpretation.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:55.030
It is therefore, important to review
everything you write before you send

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.330
it, just in case what you have written
doesn’t impart what you meant it to.

00:00:59.269 --> 00:01:04.210
It is also important that when receiving written
communication, you make sure, you take the time

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.630
to read it carefully, so you don't miss anything.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.249
Maddy: Oral communication includes
face-to-face conversations, phone calls,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.910
video calls, and giving presentations.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.580
When communicating orally you should make
sure that you speak slowly and clearly.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:26.119
You don't want the other person to mishear you,
so make sure you're being precise with your words.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:31.980
If you need to give someone a lot of
information this way, take your time, so as

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.670
not to overwhelm them by speaking too quickly.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.320
And make sure you use language and
terminology that they'll understand.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.800
Although all forms of communication
involve a back-and-forth, this is

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.049
especially true for oral communication.

00:01:47.779 --> 00:01:52.770
It is therefore important to make sure the other
person has time to reply and ask questions,

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.400
and don't assume they've understood everything.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:02.009
Gently ask them if they want you to clarify and
listen carefully to what they say at all times.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:07.160
Phillip: Nonverbal communication
means communicating "without words".

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.310
Typically, it's about body
language and appearance.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.800
It's your facial expressions, your tone of voice,
and what you're doing with your arms and legs.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.370
It's everything you're doing
except the writing or speaking.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.679
Try to be aware of things like posture and stance.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.670
It's important to appear confident and
calm, but also be wary of appearing

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.640
physically imposing or defensive.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.440
Try to be aware of your expressions too.

00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:38.040
Sometimes when we're having a difficult
conversation, it's easy to say a lot with

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.649
just how your face looks, so it’s essential
that your body language matches your words.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.240
Nonverbal communication also includes
other things like the way you dress.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.399
Think about the environment you're in
and who you're going to be speaking to,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.170
when deciding what you're going to wear.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.950
What impression are you giving with your outfit?

00:02:58.279 --> 00:03:03.600
Maddy: Visual communication is when images
or video are used to communicate information.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.790
This is often used along with words or speech.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.190
For example, including graphs
or animations in a presentation.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.040
The important thing is that the
visual element of communication

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.060
should complement the other elements.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.480
Sometimes people will include visual
elements which can distract attention

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.910
and don't enhance the message or contain
any relevant information on their own.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:31.090
Communication today has become more visual
in general, especially with the use of

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:36.180
digital media, but it is also important
that imagery is not overused, so that

00:03:36.199 --> 00:03:38.510
the message gets lost or misinterpreted.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:38.749
Phillip: Listening.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:48.581
Understanding how communication takes place can
help you to communicate more effectively, and

00:03:48.581 --> 00:03:50.950
as you learn to communicate more effectively,
you start to understand how listening

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.009
is an important part of communication.

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:58.954
Active listening is a way of effectively engaging
with those who are communicating with you and

00:03:58.954 --> 00:04:01.950
is an important part of the negotiating process.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:06.790
By letting others speak and showing that
you understand what they are saying, by

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.200
the way you respond to, both verbally
and nonverbally, helps ensure that

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.450
effective communication is taking place.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:20.380
So, we can see that communication can take place
in numerous ways but unless you understand what

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:24.520
is being communicated to you, and you can show
that you have understood that communication,

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.659
then it is not going to be effective.

